{"base_rate":0.21927374301675978,"brier":0.06766256983240224,"bss":0.604758014197327,"bss_hi":0.6911339767624566,"bss_lo":0.5144361478772393,"chart":{"base":[251.5,78.5],"fp":[263.8,314.1],"lead":"62,250.6 272,225.9 482,197.4 692,125.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.60 — higher than 98% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +3pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 47% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 7%; promised 84% → rained 81%"},"rel":"80.6,437.9 591.3,115.7"},"country":"ES","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.036145251396648065,"ess":256.5770152290838,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Sevilla</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Sevilla rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>92%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 716 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSEVILLA/SAN PABLO, 9.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.60, ranked 4 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(2&ndash;18) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>492</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Sevilla</b> <span class=\"muted\">Spain</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;22% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 22% of days.</p><p>The forecast did far better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.60</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>2&ndash;18\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>716 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Sevilla &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Sevilla\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.590121951219515,378.3008130081301 125.6792105263158,281.42105263157896 300.68666666666667,93.83333333333337 407.24894736842117,18.0 407.24894736842117,32.36842105263156 300.68666666666667,169.66666666666666 125.6792105263158,343.6842105263158 59.590121951219515,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"302.18435754189943\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"302.18435754189943\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.590121951219515,372.3821138211382 125.6792105263158,267.0526315789474 300.68666666666667,129.22222222222223 407.24894736842117,46.73684210526318\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 492 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.590121951219515\" cy=\"372.3821138211382\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"125.6792105263158\" cy=\"267.0526315789474\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 69%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"300.68666666666667\" cy=\"129.22222222222223\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 92% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.24894736842117\" cy=\"46.73684210526318\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(22%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Sevilla the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.66) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.31).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'>0.309</td><td class='num'>0.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>201</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.534</td><td class='num'>6.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.566</td><td class='num'>3.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>163</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.663</td><td class='num'>4.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":37.38283,"lon":-5.97317,"n":716,"n_cities":216,"name":"Sevilla","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.004491869918699187,"n":492,"obs":0.026422764227642278,"sig":true},{"hi":0.4,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.19118421052631582,"n":76,"obs":0.3157894736842105,"sig":true},{"hi":0.93,"lo":0.4,"mean":0.6855555555555556,"n":72,"obs":0.6944444444444444,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.93,"mean":0.9865789473684213,"n":76,"obs":0.9210526315789473,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":9.1,"provisional":false,"rank":4,"rank_hi":18.0,"rank_lo":2.0,"reliability":